# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Secrets reference for nano-kava-react-page
#
# IMPORTANT: The Cloud Functions in functions/ read these from Google Secret
# Manager (via firebase-functions `defineSecret`), NOT from a local .env at
# runtime. This file exists only to document which secrets must exist and how to
# manage them — copy it to `.env` only if you want a local scratch copy.
#
# Set / update a secret (you'll be prompted to paste the value):
#   firebase functions:secrets:set <NAME> --project nano-kava-landing-page
#
# After changing a secret, redeploy the function so it picks up the new version:
#   firebase deploy --only functions:sendContactEmail --project nano-kava-landing-page
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# SendGrid API key — transactional email (team notification + customer auto-reply).
# Sender domain enjoynano.com must be authenticated in SendGrid.
SENDGRID_API_KEY=

# Mailchimp Marketing API key — adds contact-form leads to the audience.
# Format: 32 hex chars, a dash, then the data center, e.g. abc123...def-us21
# Mailchimp: profile icon → Account & billing → Extras → API keys → Create A Key
MAILCHIMP_API_KEY=

# Mailchimp Audience (List) ID that leads are added to.
# Mailchimp: Audience → Settings → Audience name and defaults → Audience ID
MAILCHIMP_AUDIENCE_ID=


# Google AI (Gemini) API key from Google AI Studio — powers the Bula chat widget.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
#
# This is the ONE secret that is also read from a local `.env` at dev time: the
# Vite dev server mounts /api/chat so `make preview` works without the Firebase
# emulator. Copy this file to `.env` and paste the key to test locally.
#
# For production it must ALSO live in Secret Manager:
#   firebase functions:secrets:set GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY --project nano-kava-landing-page
#   firebase deploy --only functions:chat --project nano-kava-landing-page
GOOGLE_AI_API_KEY=